// Members (`level members …`): what applies a rule, around a node (`applied_of`); a node's members, or what a rule's
// holes hold, as entries of a name and a value (but its key and input); whether a pattern catches all (a field, or a
// sequence of one); a member set, in a node (itself, copied) and in a pattern's fields of that name; an entry; a key
// added to a node's rules (the rules' epoch moved on where it is read from).
Members := class {
  static applied_of (x) => {
    a := x
    while (a != None) && ((a is Applied) == 0) {
