// Calls (`level calls …`): a function called with none, one or two arguments (in the arguments shared for that, when
// it is the language's own: a closure, curried or applied), a member called so (its own closure, else what it is);
// those of a list a function picks; a member mapped (`map`, of a text or a structure); a place of a name; what a key
// reads of a text (its length and whether it is wholly noted on it); a name's number and its text; an argument.
Calls := class {
  static direct (c) => (c is Closure) || (c is Curried) || (c is Applied)
